bodyHtml: |
  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Until this summer, Saint-Raphaël's supervised beaches were off-limits to dogs in the bathing season, even on a leash. For summer 2026, the town opened a "caniplage" on Beaurivage beach, next to the Diana jetty, right in the town centre; Nice-Matin (17 July 2026) describes it as accessible until 30 September.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>Estérel Côte d'Azur confirms that Beau Rivage is among the beaches for dogs, while the supervised beaches and several other Saint-Raphaël sites remain off-limits to dogs in the bathing season. At the opening, it was announced that dogs had to stay on a leash, that category 1 and 2 dogs were excluded and that identification was required; these details could not be re-checked. As the 2026 season ended on 30 September, the area is probably no longer open: check with the town hall (04 94 82 15 00) before coming, and to find out whether the arrangement will be renewed.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: in the meantime, Plage du Pacha in Fréjus, cited by Nice-Matin as an alternative, is a neighbouring dog beach.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Saint-Raphaël's town centre, its shops and its seafront promenade are steps away.</p>
